<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">Reconciliation: Exchanges in Grief</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;While reconstruction continues and the BFS keep daydreaming about their coming roadtrip, trouble builds and ominous signs further threaten their plans for the future.&lt;br /&gt;Adora's relationship with She-Ra is shifting, and Entrapta can do little about a situation that's hurting them both. Catra knows she must reconcile with her time in the war and find a meaningful path forward, and unresolved issues create strains in her relationship with Adora. Hordak struggles to comprehend the pain he's caused and faces Mermista's and Micah's grief in turn while the alliance gets used to having him around. Unfortunately, he's so busy with the past that it clouds his ability to navigate the present, complicating things between Entrapta and himself.&lt;br /&gt;Meanwhile, news filtering in from other worlds in combination with what they're learning from the clones paints an ever darker picture of the universe just outside their orbit, but the alliance starts to wonder if their deadliest threat is from within, rather than from our space. They can all sense big events headed their way, but the alliance is, for the most part, still flying blind.&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>AintGonnaHauntItself</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
      </dc:creator>
